 "title": "PLOS Biology and PLOS ONE Collaboration",
 "summary": "PLOS Biology and PLOS ONE are two entities that collaborate in the publication of scientific research. PLOS Biology conceptualizes research with Green Robin, while PLOS ONE publishes papers with Arthur J. Lustig as editor. PLOS ONE Editorial Office Staff manages the publication process, including making data available. PLOS Data policy requires authors to share data and code. PLOS Biology and PLOS ONE are both published by PLOS, which is led by Roland G Roberts. PLOS ONE also publishes papers on topics such as budding yeast and hydrogen sulfide gas.",
